# Vue Frontend (`apps/web`)

## Template library (mandatory)

There is **one** public UI surface: `@/ui` (primitives + app chrome).

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { Button, PageBody, PageHeader, DataList } from '@/ui'
</script>

<!-- ❌ BAD — deep imports / rogue chrome -->
import { Button } from '@/ui/button'
import PageBody from '@/components/PageBody.vue'
```

- Primitives live under `src/ui/{name}/`
- Chrome implementations live under `src/components/` but are **only** consumed via `@/ui`
- Library internals may deep-import (`@/ui/button`) to avoid circular barrels
- Add UI only through the `add-shadcn-component` skill (primitive or chrome path)
- Canon: `apps/web/src/ui/README.md`

## Components

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref } from 'vue'
import type { User } from '@/api/types/schema'

interface Props {
  user: User
}
const props = defineProps<Props>()
</script>
```

- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` for all new components
- Views: `*View.vue` in `src/views/`
- Absolute imports via `@/`

## Styling (compose only — do not invent looks in features)

Visual style lives in three places only:

1. `src/styles/theme.css` — Brand block (`--brand*`) + semantic tokens
2. `@/ui` primitives — component variants / focus / sizes
3. `@/ui` chrome (implemented in `src/components/`) — page body, lists, form panels, shell

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD — view invents card / color look -->
<div class="rounded-lg border bg-card p-6 text-[#1b4332]">…</div>
<Button class="bg-green-700">Save</Button>

<!-- ✅ GOOD — compose chrome + tokens -->
<PageBody>
  <PageHeader title="Users" />
  <StatusMessage v-if="error" tone="error">{{ error }}</StatusMessage>
  <DataList>…</DataList>
</PageBody>
```

- Re-skin the product by editing `--brand*` in `theme.css` only
- Need a new look? Add/extend `@/ui` — never style in the view
- No hex/rgb, no arbitrary colors, no inline `style`, no restyling primitives from features
- ESLint enforces import + style fences on `src/views/**`, `src/modules/**`, `App.vue`

## Imports

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — external first, then @/
import { computed } from 'vue'
import { Button, PageBody } from '@/ui'
import { authApi } from '@/api/authApi'
```

## API calls in views

Use API modules / stores — do not call `fetch` directly in views.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const res = await fetch('/api/v1/auth/me')

// ✅ GOOD
const user = await authApi.me()
```
